  "reviewed_arguments": [
    "The theorem assumes a scalar classical operator of any real order on a general smooth manifold, with nonzero complex bracket on its entire characteristic set. No global lower bound or noncompact global L2 boundedness is assumed.",
    "The operator class includes the full diagonal kernel relation, with both zero-covector axes excluded. Proper composition, adjunction and the genuine smoothing ideal are justified by the exact earlier Fourier-kernel action proof.",
    "The Gaussian Weyl symbol is computed directly, with its factor two, both frequency signs and spectator variables. All balanced shell derivatives are controlled.",
    "The exact regularized Weyl product gives a commutator estimate using only positive derivatives of the slow factor. Full integrations by parts, left-symbol conversion and the finite-seminorm packet theorem avoid a formal decreasing-order expansion at the critical scaling.",
    "Balanced dilation gives the half-order improvement. Remote shell blocks have both rapid Schur marginals; finite overlap and weighted summation prove every real Sobolev estimate, uniformly for ordinary symbol families.",
    "Full Egorov transports the bound through graph conjugation. Adjoints, ordinary cutoffs, finite products and half-order remainders preserve the estimate.",
    "The partition is placed on the left near positive characteristics and on the right near negative characteristics. Larger cutoff errors are smoothing. The proper locally finite construction has genuine zero-order defects and retains the exact inverse gain.",
    "Disjoint characteristic relations prove both annihilation identities, idempotence and the reflexive inverse identity modulo smooth kernels. A finite-order improvement is not substituted for a smoothing error.",
    "A compactly localized positive bounded operator has an actual L2 inverse. Uniform regularizers and finite half-order bootstrap prove every positive Sobolev order; self-adjoint duality gives all negative orders.",
    "Nested conic estimates prove pseudolocality of that inverse. A separate uniform annular iteration proves rapid decay near both kernel axes. Compact input/output support is established from the equation and adjunction.",
    "Overlap uniqueness and a proper locally finite partition assemble the local positive inverses into a two-sided global inverse modulo smooth kernels. Adjunction gives its Hermitian property in the same quotient.",
    "Ordered algebra normalizes the kernel range and the adjoint cokernel range separately. Both corrected inverse identities, both annihilation identities and the unchanged Sobolev gain are proved.",
    "Exact wavefront equalities follow from the earlier arbitrary-regularity nonsolvability result, the adjoint bracket sign and density of the elliptic complement. Empty sign regions and an empty characteristic set are included.",
    "The uniqueness proof compares Hermitian projectors and then factors the inverse difference through the two disjoint sign regions. Its proper pseudolocal class is stated explicitly; arbitrary nonlocal additions are addressed in a solved exercise.",
    "Thirty-seven exact algebra and scale checks support the analytic proofs. The 268 formulae, 20 displays, eleven overlapping desktop captures, complete figure and two mobile samples were inspected. All three exercises have complete solutions.",
    "The final global assembly and Hermitian normalization assertion of H4 Section 26.3 now has a receiving proof. Earlier numbered results remain preserved. Later sections, other course obligations and internal foundation closure remain active."
  ],
